---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Matrix from '../ui/Matrix.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s44c-exec-vs-debug"
  chapter="Advanced Debugging"
  title="exec vs kubectl debug"
  track="core"
  notes="exec = quick read-only-ish check in existing container. debug = ephemeral toolbox without baking tools into the app image. Neither is step 1."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <Matrix
      headers={['Tool', 'Use when', 'Avoid when']}
      rows={[
        ['kubectl exec', 'Quick file/env/port check in running container', 'CrashLoop (no running process), hardened images, need tcpdump'],
        ['kubectl debug (ephemeral)', 'Need netshoot tools / share namespaces', 'Before describe/events; unrestricted prod without audit'],
        ['debug node / hostNetwork', 'Node-level CNI / kubelet networking', 'First reflex — high blast radius'],
      ]}
    />
    <Callout type="danger">
      Invasive debugging is not triage. describe → events → logs first; then exec/debug with a hypothesis.
    </Callout>
  </div>
</Slide>
